        <tr><td colspan=2>
		    <br>
		    Bands childhood was spent in training with the great “Holy Elven Masters”.  Her mother, Frionia tried to teach her some melee disciplines, but the young Band seemed uninterested.  She preferred to sit and pray during battle,  unleashing Tunare’s awesome power, on friends and foes alike, but only when needed.  Tunare blessed Band, like her daughter Frionia, with the same gift of “Eternal Ageless Beauty”.  Frionia often thought the resemblance between her daughter and her mother was uncanny. It also seemed the same “Narcissistic” traits of Tunare where obviously passed on to Band.<br>
<br>
Band is not afraid to announce her Divine Lineage to complete strangers.  To her mothers dismay, Band has also taken a strong interest in males, yet another trait passed on by Tunare. Being the first High-Elf ever to explore Antonica, she has especially taken a liking to both Human and Barbarian males, which again has not only her mother up in arms, but the entire “Holy Council”.  When the Council questions Band about these “indulgences” she often responds, “You dare question the daughter of Tunare.”  The conversation usually ends at this point.  How can one argue with a creature who has a Gods blood running through her veins?<br>
<br>
To make matters worse Band’s mother Frionia, recently had an entire city named after her in the new Continent of Kunark.   Band, who hates boat travel, demanded that the King of Felwithe build an enormous boat that would expedite the travel time between Faydwer and Kunark.  The Boat, and engineering masterpiece was finally built at an enormous expense.<br>
<br>
Band’s life has not been as easy as some may believe. Recently, Innoruk’s minions struck down the Healer with a hideous plague.  She was bedridden for months – not even Tunare herself could cure this hideous disease. The disease, finally, ran its course and Band returned to her duties.  She has watched many children, that were once her junior, become great leaders in their own right. She has witnessed the Kings own daughter, Aaylia, grow from a young priest into a powerful Vicar.  Surprisingly, Band is quite proud of her peers accomplishments.  <br>
<br>
Despite all of Bands negative traits she has a very kind heart.  She is regarded with great respect for Clerical abilities.  She often spends several weeks on Holy Missions helping less-seasoned adventures by bestowing the power of Tunare into them, and healing their broken bodies.  She now strives to fulfill her destiny which is to destroy the evil Innoruk and help bring peace to Norrath.<br>
